1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:06,700
Most study tools make the student adapt to a workflow.
A real tutor does the opposite.

2
00:00:07,350 --> 00:00:14,000
You can begin with whatever is true right now:
“I have ten minutes. Help me understand heart valves.”

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:21,700
The tutor notices the time, the goal, and the material you already have.
No setup wizard. No rigid lesson plan.

4
00:00:22,350 --> 00:00:29,600
Before it teaches, the harness locks
a trusted snapshot of your source.

5
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:37,700
It asks the one question that matters next—and changes direction
without losing context.

6
00:00:38,350 --> 00:00:44,800
Now the lesson becomes a loop.
Explain one idea from the source. Test it immediately.

7
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:56,700
Record what the student understood, and schedule what should return later.
The conversation stays flexible; the learning state keeps accumulating.

8
00:00:57,350 --> 00:01:04,800
Underneath, every transition is an append-only event.
Pause, resume, or change models.

9
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:11,700
The same continuation can be replayed and verified.
Skills carry behavior. Provider adapters stay replaceable.

10
00:01:12,350 --> 00:01:19,700
Study Agent Harness.
Let the tutor adapt. Keep the learning durable.
